#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a7084c-c30f-5232-858b-9de95f8dc7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266605} {:answer/id #uuid "7035ae25-bae6-5784-9a22-06a21aa5b21d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267131} {:answer/id #uuid "8b24fe95-3529-5193-be67-e03845cb8972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X{X}^{T}\\,(X{X}^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267393} {:answer/id #uuid "d598c94a-a6a6-575e-afa4-7a9765d0b575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}X{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268047} {:answer/id #uuid "e18490b8-96ff-50e6-aa1e-707f1e27022c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}^{T}\\,(X{X}^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267131} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcc1a7f0-9292-56fb-b1bc-1ef776adae4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268743}] :question/id #uuid "d4d90bb0-89dc-5241-a5f2-d53a62426c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139594" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-3$ | $1$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\beta =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\nX\\beta =y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459b6282-6263-541f-95e0-265ac1712a9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}Xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266764} {:answer/id #uuid "651d2504-9596-5365-b8f7-f022fa03ab5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267040} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d9a9ae-7c5e-50d3-acd2-07abe3bc2029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X{X}^{T})^{-1}Xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267793} {:answer/id #uuid "d5db1c2b-057f-518d-8062-a96aafa91dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X{X}^{T})^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268049} {:answer/id #uuid "dacc5347-1a2a-56f9-8602-42c0fddffec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X{X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267040} :answer-field/id #uuid "40056ea3-e92f-5739-affc-b7d0de6feb4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268514}] :question/id #uuid "6718ccea-1d8f-5299-bcfe-0f7e85cd7d04" :question/math-academy-id "q-139595" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-3$ | $2$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 7 & {7}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 9 & {9}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\beta =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\nX\\beta =y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "362a79c7-8381-508d-a693-01e846420040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}^{T}\\,(X{X}^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266612} {:answer/id #uuid "39348ecb-402a-5f85-b880-7dce810e3a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X{X}^{T})^{-1}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266644} {:answer/id #uuid "7b909b46-e322-5637-be92-6d173e2f06a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267238} {:answer/id #uuid "b2edbebe-22f4-52c7-a31a-a8d199495e56" :answer/type {:db/id